Inhabitants(pure-Fallen-Angels, Fallen-Angel-related-races, half-Fallen-Angels);
Demographics(half-Fallen-Angels(born-between-Fallen-Angels-and-other-races));

Cocytus: AKA Ice Hell;
Location: deepest part of Underworld, connected to Realm of the Dead;
Function: prison(for powerful/dangerous figures, those who committed gravest sins/betrayals), home(rare/dangerous creatures);
Notable inhabitants/features: Pale Horse;
Description: "cruelest depths of Hell", eternal binding of prisoners;

Dimension Blade: AKA Michi no Jigen-tō, high-tier Sacred Gear/potential mid-tier Longinus;
Dormant-Manifestations: intuitive-mastery(striking angles, precision), unconscious-ability(detect/exploit weaknesses), extended-strikes(beyond physical reach), spatial-distortions(subtle shifts), blue-energy-flashes(during intense training);
Awakened-Powers: cutting-ability(virtually any material/barrier), dimensional-slashes(distant targets), techniques(require physical conditioning, demonic power mastery), Judgment-Cut(master-level technique, space manipulation, multi-target striking, high-speed attack), Judgment-Cut-End(50m radius time-stop, 5-second duration, faster-than-time movement, absolute slash control, instant silent teleportation), spatial-portals(open/collapse), dimensional-barrier-cutting;
Balance-Breaker: user-gear-merger(near-unlimited demonic power, body-limited), invisible-sword-attacks(300-meter radius), domain-effects(time-slowdown, instant teleportation, sword-attack manifestation, gravity manipulation), duration(linked to demonic power, body limits);
Appearance: blade(traditional katana, prominent hamon), handle(diamond-pattern tsukamaki, gold dragon menuki), handguard(octagonal tsuba, gold/navy-blue designs, triangular three-circle clusters), scabbard(black lacquered wood, metallic accents, sageo cord);
Additional-Notes: dormancy(within user's body, unmanifested until awakening), manifestation(summonable at will), resonance(with user's natural talents), awakening(gradual process), value(target for multiple factions), detection(unusual presence sensed but unidentified), concealment(hidden from supernatural detection)
